Branding is not in this repository.

The page references three files that are supplied at deploy time and are
gitignored:

    logo.png              shown left of the heading, any aspect, ~400px wide is fine
    favicon.png           32x32, browser tab
    apple-touch-icon.png  180x180, iOS home screen

Generate the two icons from the logo by padding it onto a transparent square,
so a wide mark is not squashed into the tab slot:

    python3 - <<'PY'
    from PIL import Image
    im = Image.open("logo.png").convert("RGBA")
    side = max(im.size)
    sq = Image.new("RGBA", (side, side), (0, 0, 0, 0))
    sq.paste(im, ((side - im.size[0]) // 2, (side - im.size[1]) // 2), im)
    sq.resize((32, 32), Image.LANCZOS).save("favicon.png")
    sq.resize((180, 180), Image.LANCZOS).save("apple-touch-icon.png")
    PY

If the files are absent the page still works. The img carries alt="" so it
degrades to a gap rather than a broken-image icon, and the tab falls back to the
browser default.

Nothing on the running site depends on this repository: it is served from
/var/lib/pool-web/www, which is a copy. Deleting this repo does not affect the
dashboard.
